sequenceDiagram
    participant C as 🌐 Client (Web/Android)
    participant API as 🔧 Express REST API
    participant AUTH as 🔐 Auth Middleware
    participant SVC as ⚙️ Service Layer
    participant DB as 🗃️ PostgreSQL (Prisma)
    participant AI as 🤖 AI Provider (OpenAI)

    Note over C,DB: Auth Flow
    C->>API: POST /api/auth/login {email, password}
    API->>SVC: authService.login()
    SVC->>DB: SELECT user WHERE email=?
    DB-->>SVC: User record
    SVC->>SVC: bcrypt.compare(password, hash)
    SVC-->>API: JWT token + user
    API-->>C: { success: true, data: { token, user } }

    Note over C,DB: Protected Ride Booking Flow
    C->>API: POST /api/rides/book {pickup, destination, rideType, driverId}
    API->>AUTH: authenticate(req) — verify JWT Bearer
    AUTH->>DB: verify token signature + user exists
    AUTH-->>API: req.user = { id, role }
    API->>SVC: rideService.bookRide(userId, data)
    SVC->>SVC: calculateEstimatedFare(pickup, dest, type)
    SVC->>DB: INSERT INTO rides {userId, driverId, pin, fareEstimate...}
    DB-->>SVC: Created ride record
    SVC-->>API: ride with driver + vehicle
    API-->>C: { success: true, data: ride }

    Note over C,DB: AI Chat Flow
    C->>API: POST /api/ai/chat {message, sessionId?}
    API->>AUTH: authenticate(req)
    AUTH-->>API: req.user
    API->>SVC: aiService.handleChat(userId, message)
    SVC->>DB: Get or create ChatSession
    SVC->>DB: INSERT ChatMessage (role=USER)
    alt AI_API_KEY configured
        SVC->>AI: POST /v1/chat/completions {model: gpt-4o-mini}
        AI-->>SVC: AI response text
    else No API key (default)
        SVC->>SVC: generateKnowledgeResponse(query)\nRule-based contextual engine
    end
    SVC->>DB: INSERT ChatMessage (role=ASSISTANT, content=reply)
    SVC-->>API: { sessionId, reply, createdAt }
    API-->>C: { success: true, data: result }

    Note over C,DB: Cross-Platform Sync
    C->>API: PATCH /api/tasks/:id {status: COMPLETED}
    API->>AUTH: authenticate
    AUTH-->>API: req.user
    API->>SVC: taskService.update(userId, taskId, data)
    SVC->>DB: UPDATE tasks SET status=COMPLETED
    DB-->>SVC: Updated task
    SVC-->>API: task
    API-->>C: { success: true, data: task }
    Note over C: ✅ Web AND Android see same updated task
